Prevention and Protection Against Social Engineering
How to Prevent Social Engineering
Never share passwords with other people.
Verify the identity of people requesting sensitive information.
Avoid clicking suspicious links.
Enable Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA).
Keep software and security systems updated.
Be careful when sharing personal information online.
Report suspicious emails, calls and activities.
Follow workplace security policies.
Employee Responsibilities
Employees should:

Protect confidential company information.
Attend cybersecurity awareness training.
Follow access control procedures.
Report suspicious activities immediately.
Avoid allowing unknown individuals into restricted areas.
Conclusion
Preventing social engineering requires awareness, caution and responsible behaviour. Everyone has a role to play in protecting information and computer systems.
